  "content": {
    "title": "'Scarpetta' Season 2 Will Adapt Patricia Cornwell’s 'The Body Farm' and 'Cruel and Unusual'",
    "text": "\"Hearst Magazines and Yahoo may earn commission or revenue on some items through these links.\"Dr. Kay Scarpetta’s work is far from done. There are more murder mysteries left for the medical examiner to solve, and she’ll put her deductive skills to the test in Scarpetta season 2.The Prime Video series, executive produced by Nicole Kidman and Jamie Lee Curtis—who respectively star in the show as Scarpetta and her sister, Dorothy—received an automatic season 2 greenlight with the news of its arrival in September 2024. Deadline reported that the streaming platform ordered two seasons of the show, which is based on author Patricia Cornwell’s bestselling book series of the same name.Connie Chornuk“I’m beyond excited that this is finally happening. This will be great fun for all, and I’m grateful for the immense talent that the show is drawing,” Cornwell told Deadline in a statement. “I’ve always been a huge fan of Jamie Lee Curtis and Nicole Kidman. Their wanting to do this is humbling and simply awesome. Working with the brilliant [writer] Liz Sarnoff is amazing. Blumhouse and Prime Video are a dream. This has been worth waiting for, and I’m so looking forward to the show.”The author also told ELLE in November 2025 that she has attempted to bring Scarpetta to the screen “since the beginning of my career.” Cornwell added, “That long road of disappointments has turned into something so worth waiting for and beyond my biggest dreams.”Here’s everything we know about Scarpetta season 2.What will Scarpetta season 2 be about?The second season of Scarpetta will adapt Cornwell’s Cruel and Unusual and The Body Farm, showrunner Liza Sarnoff revealed in an interview with The Hollywood Reporter.“Season two picks up pretty soon after the events of episode eight of season one [the finale] in the present day. In the past, it picks up a little bit later. Because we were able to reveal the murder in episode seven, we were able to resolve all that stuff. But because the emotional storytelling is the key to the present, we didn’t want to miss a lot of the aftermath of that,” she shared. “We do two books a season—season one, we did Postmortem and Autopsy, and this year we’re doing Cruel and Unusual and The Body Farm. So the stories definitely start to pick up, and murders happen. Cruel and Unusual, [set] in the past, is a story that involves a prisoner who’s executed, so it gives us a different setting to roll into at the top of the season.”Sarnoff explained that she landed on Cruel and Unusual and The Body Farm for season 2 because the books felt like a match thematically. “I thought these two really speak to each other, and it’ll be really interesting if we can make them work together,” she added. “I didn’t want to get too far into the series—those are actually books four and five of [Cornwell’s] series—so I took a step back from the present day books and thought, ‘Let’s do a past book with the present-day cast.’”As for the plot, season 2 of Scarpetta will pick up right where the show left off—with Dr. Kay beating Ryan to death, and leaving viewers on a cliffhanger by not showing who opened up the door in the final moment of the finale episode.Connie ChornukThe synopses for Cruel and Unusual and The Body Farm also offer more clues to what fans can expect from season 2 of Scarpetta.The Cruel and Unusual synopsis reads: “Killing me won’t kill the beast” are the last words of rapist-murderer Ronnie Joe Waddell, written four days before his execution. But they can’t explain how medical examiner Dr. Kay Scarpetta finds Waddell’s fingerprints on another crime scene—after she’d performed his autopsy. If this is some sort of game, Scarpetta seems to be the target. And if the next victim is someone she knows, the punishment will be cruel and unusual...”Shop NowPocket Books Cruel and Unusual: Scarpetta 4 (Kay Scarpetta)amazon.com$6.94The synopsis for The Body Farm reads: “Little Emily Steiner left a church meeting late one afternoon and strolled toward home along a lakeside path; a week later, her nude body was discovered, bound in blaze-orange duct tape. Called by the North Carolina authorities, forensic pathologist Kay Scarpetta recognizes similarities to the gruesome work of a serial killer who has long eluded the FBI. But as she tries to make sense of the evidence, she is left with questions that lead her to the Body Farm, a little-known research facility in Tennessee where, with the help of some grisly experiments, she might discover the answer.“It is Scarpetta alone who can interpret the forensic hieroglyphics that eventually reveal a solution to the case as staggering as it is horrifying. But she must also endeavor to help her niece, Lucy, who is embroiled in controversy at Quantico. And Scarpetta, too, is vulnerable, as she opens herself to the first physical and emotional bond she has felt in far too long a time. Tenacious and brilliant, tender and gentle, this is Scarpetta even more realized and poignant than we’ve seen her before.”Shop NowThe Body Farm: Scarpetta 5 (Kay Scarpetta)amazon.com$9.99Who is in the cast?Kidman and Curtis will reprise their roles as Scarpetta and Dorothy. According to Deadline’s September 2024 report, the series will see its regulars returning as well:Ariana DeBose as Lucy Farinelli-Watson, Dorothy’s daughterBobby Cannavale as former detective Pete MarinoSimon Baker as FBI profiler Benton WesleyRosy McEwen as Past Kay ScarpettaJake Cannavale as Past Pete MarinoWhat has the cast said about Scarpetta?In ELLE’s exclusive look at Scarpetta season 1, Kidman gushed over the foresight exhibited in Cornwell’s writing, all while keeping the plot as scientific as possible.“I love where Patricia’s imagination goes in her writing, that she really doubles down on wild storylines, but stays scientific,” she said. “There are things like AI bots that Patricia explored years ago. The books are cutting-edge, just a tiny bit sci-fi in the crime mystery genre.”Courtesy Prime VideoKidman further noted that she thought the character of Scarpetta would be “fascinating and scary onscreen—exploring cases through the lens of a slightly rogue medical examiner. We tried to adapt them to film years ago, but serializing them was the way to go.” Finding out that Curtis was also playing a part in the series further cemented her interest in bringing the story to life. “I was in,” she added. “Jamie is an inspiring force of nature—brilliant and hilarious—and I’ve loved watching where life has taken her. I very much wanted to work with her.”Curtis was equally excited to work with Kidman on the show: “Although I have a small part, that sister relationship is very important to the show,” she said. “And I’m just thrilled that now I get to act opposite Nicole Kidman, when in fact, I just thought I was going to be [a producer].”Following the season 1 finale, Baker shared his thoughts on what he hopes will happen in season 2. “I’ve read the first two episodes for next season, and there’s a lot of trying to reconnect again,” he told The Hollywood Reporter in March 2026. “Between Kay and I, there’s a fair bit of fallout about that divorce conversation, which I think is the last time we’re together in that [finale].”Bobby Cannavale revealed he wants “to see more of Pete and Benton.” He told the outlet, “I do wonder, with what Benton is going through now in particular—Pete seems to ask a lot about what’s going on with Kay, and I don’t think that’s purely for his own [selfish] reasons. I think he and Benton are good friends, so I’d like to see that relationship deepen a little bit more…I just hope that Marino and Kay get closer to whatever their catharsis is going to be for each other emotionally without actually getting there.”When will Scarpetta season 2 come out?The release date has not yet been announced. If we are to look at past seasons for reference, Scarpetta season 1 arrived on March 11, 2026, a year and five months after Deadline reported the show received a green light in September 2024.You Might Also Like",
